---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | DHPMCC">
  <section id="privacy-policy" class="content-container policy-section">
    <header class="policy-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">DHPMCC Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle"><em>Last Updated: September 2026</em></p>
    </header>

    <div class="policy-preamble">
      <p>
        The Daniel H. Plotnick Memorial Computing Competition (DHPMCC) respects the privacy of participants, coaches, teachers, volunteers, and visitors to the DHPMCC website.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information DHPMCC may collect, how that information may be used, when it may be shared, how it may be protected, and how individuals may contact DHPMCC regarding their information.
      </p>
      <p>
        DHPMCC may be hosted at Bergen County Academies (BCA). Information collected in connection with the competition may therefore also be subject to applicable Bergen County Technical Schools and BCA policies and requirements. Where those policies impose additional requirements, they control.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="policy-toc" aria-label="Table of Contents">
      <span class="toc-label">Jump to section:</span>
      <ul class="toc-list">
        <li><a href="#info-collect">1. Information We Collect</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-use">2. How We Use Information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#results">3. Competition Results</a></li>
        <li><a href="#minors">4. Minors</a></li>
        <li><a href="#recordings">5. Photographs &amp; Recordings</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sharing">6. Information Sharing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#submissions">7. Contest Submissions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#retention">8. Data Retention</a></li>
        <li><a href="#security">9. Security</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cookies">10. Cookies &amp; Technical Info</a></li>
        <li><a href="#external-services">11. External Websites &amp; Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#privacy-requests">12. Access, Correction &amp; Requests</a></li>
        <li><a href="#policy-changes">13. Changes to This Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">14. Contact</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="policy-body">
      <section id="info-collect" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>Depending on how a person interacts with DHPMCC, we may collect information such as:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Name.</li>
          <li>Grade or school year.</li>
          <li>School or educational institution.</li>
          <li>Division or competition category.</li>
          <li>Email address or other contact information.</li>
          <li>Registration information.</li>
          <li>Contest submissions and associated submission information.</li>
          <li>Contest scores, rankings, and results.</li>
          <li>Information voluntarily provided when contacting organizers.</li>
          <li>Technical information generated when using DHPMCC websites or systems, such as IP addresses, timestamps, browser information, and server logs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>DHPMCC seeks to collect only information reasonably necessary to operate, administer, secure, and improve the competition.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="how-use" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">2. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may use collected information to:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Register participants.</li>
          <li>Organize divisions and competition logistics.</li>
          <li>Administer, judge, and score submissions.</li>
          <li>Communicate with participants, coaches, teachers, and supervising adults about the competition.</li>
          <li>Publish competition results where appropriate.</li>
          <li>Maintain competition records.</li>
          <li>Investigate rule violations or security incidents.</li>
          <li>Protect the security and integrity of DHPMCC systems.</li>
          <li>Respond to questions, requests, or reports.</li>
          <li>Comply with applicable legal, school, or administrative requirements.</li>
          <li>Improve the DHPMCC website and competition.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>DHPMCC will not use participant information for unrelated commercial advertising or sell participant personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="results" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">3. Competition Results</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may publish competition results, including information such as a participant’s name, school, division, placement, score, or award.</p>
        <p>Because DHPMCC is a competition, some information about results may need to be publicly available to maintain a meaningful and verifiable record of the event.</p>
        <p>Where appropriate and permitted by applicable BCA policies, DHPMCC may use a participant’s name in connection with competition results, awards, or event recognition.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC will not intentionally publish unnecessary personal information such as home addresses, personal telephone numbers, passwords, or other sensitive information.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="minors" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">4. Minors</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may be attended and participated in by minors.</p>
        <p>We recognize that information concerning minors requires additional care. DHPMCC will collect and use participant information only for legitimate competition, educational, administrative, safety, security, or legal purposes.</p>
        <p>Where BCA, Bergen County Technical Schools, or applicable law requires parental or guardian consent, school authorization, or another form of permission, DHPMCC will follow the applicable process.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC does not knowingly use children’s personal information for behavioral advertising or sell children’s personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="recordings" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">5. Photographs and Recordings</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC or authorized event personnel may photograph or record the event for legitimate educational, archival, informational, or promotional purposes, subject to applicable BCA policies and required permissions.</p>
        <p>Photographs or recordings may appear on DHPMCC or BCA-related websites, publications, or other official communications where permitted.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC will make reasonable efforts to handle photographs and recordings in accordance with applicable school policies and permissions.</p>
        <p>Requests or concerns regarding photographs or recordings may be directed to the DHPMCC organizers.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">6. Information Sharing</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may share information with:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Authorized DHPMCC organizers, judges, volunteers, and administrators who need the information to perform their responsibilities.</li>
          <li>Authorized BCA or Bergen County Technical Schools personnel when necessary to administer the event or comply with school requirements.</li>
          <li>Service providers that operate infrastructure used by DHPMCC, such as hosting, database, email, registration, authentication, or security services, when reasonably necessary to provide those services.</li>
          <li>Parents, guardians, coaches, or teachers when appropriate and permitted in connection with competition administration.</li>
          <li>Governmental, legal, or emergency authorities when required by law or necessary to protect safety, rights, or security.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>DHPMCC does not sell personal information.</p>
        <p>Third-party services used by DHPMCC may process information according to their own privacy policies and applicable agreements.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="submissions" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">7. Contest Submissions</h2>
        <p>Programs and other materials submitted for competition may be stored by DHPMCC for judging, scoring, auditing, security, dispute resolution, and archival purposes.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC may retain submissions and associated metadata for as long as reasonably necessary to maintain accurate competition records and verify results.</p>
        <p>Unless otherwise stated in the Competition Rules, submitting a program to DHPMCC does not by itself transfer ownership of the participant’s underlying intellectual property to DHPMCC.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC may reproduce or display submissions when reasonably necessary to administer, judge, document, or promote the competition, subject to applicable policies and permissions.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">8. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC retains information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Policy, legitimate competition records, security, dispute resolution, archival purposes, or applicable legal and school requirements.</p>
        <p>Different types of information may therefore be retained for different periods.</p>
        <p>Competition results and historical records may be retained for substantially longer than operational information because they document the history and outcomes of the competition.</p>
        <p>When information is no longer reasonably necessary, DHPMCC may delete, anonymize, or otherwise securely dispose of it, subject to applicable BCA and district requirements.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="security" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">9. Security</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC uses reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures intended to protect information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.</p>
        <p>No website or electronic system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
        <p>Access to non-public participant information should be limited to authorized individuals who need it for legitimate DHPMCC or BCA purposes.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">10. Cookies and Technical Information</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC websites may use cookies, local storage, server logs, or similar technical mechanisms when reasonably necessary to operate, secure, or improve the website.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC does not intend to use tracking technologies for unrelated behavioral advertising.</p>
        <p>Third-party services embedded in or used by the website may independently collect technical information according to their own policies.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="external-services" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">11. External Websites and Services</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may link to or use third-party services for registration, hosting, authentication, communications, maps, code execution, or other competition functions.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC is not responsible for the privacy practices of websites or services that it does not operate.</p>
        <p>Users should review the privacy policies of third-party services before providing information to them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy-requests" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">12. Access, Correction, and Privacy Requests</h2>
        <p>Questions or requests concerning personal information collected by DHPMCC may be directed to the DHPMCC organizers.</p>
        <p>Depending on the type of information and applicable BCA or district requirements, DHPMCC may be able to provide access to, correct, or delete information.</p>
        <p>Some information may need to be retained for legitimate competition, security, legal, archival, or school purposes.</p>
        <p>Requests involving records maintained by BCA or Bergen County Technical Schools may need to be handled through the applicable school or district process.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="policy-changes" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may update this Privacy Policy when its systems, competition procedures, or applicable requirements change.</p>
        <p>The updated version will be published on the DHPMCC website with a revised “Last Updated” date.</p>
        <p>Material changes will be communicated through appropriate DHPMCC channels when reasonably necessary.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">14. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions regarding this Privacy Policy or DHPMCC’s handling of information should be directed to the official DHPMCC organizers or the appropriate BCA contact.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC will make reasonable efforts to respond to privacy concerns and requests in a timely manner.</p>
        <div class="policy-notice">
          <p>This Privacy Policy does not replace or supersede applicable Bergen County Technical Schools, Bergen County Academies, or legal requirements concerning student records, privacy, safety, or information security.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-section {
    padding-top: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    color: #555555;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .policy-preamble {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy-preamble p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .policy-toc {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .toc-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111111;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .toc-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .toc-list a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: var(--color-link-hover);
  }

  .policy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.25rem;
  }

  .policy-block {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-section-title {
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .policy-block p {
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .policy-list {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .policy-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .policy-notice {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border-left: 3px solid #8b0000;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #4a5568;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .policy-notice p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
